{
  "archgram": 1,
  "title": "How an answer comes to be",
  "description": "Before use, npm run generate has Gemini write 30 CV PDFs; npm run index has Gemini extract a profile from each, the field check locates every fact in the text so each has a page, and each chunk is embedded into Pinecone. At question time the chat screen sends the question and history to POST /api/ask, whose prompt holds no CV text. Gemini runs a tool-calling loop: three exact tools read the index, search_cv_text embeds the query and fuses BM25 with the vectors. The loop ends with present; the answer check keeps only the candidates and pages the tools returned, and the answer streams to the chat, whose source links open the PDF at the cited page.",
